{"action_id":"action.9893f50e1fff46d7a75daa9c32c7c6c9","provenance":{"allowance_slot":15,"cli_version":"codex-cli 0.153.4","configuration":"ignore-user-config; read-only; tools-disabled; no-resume","events_jsonl":"{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a0ccd3-c425-70c2-9b0d-cfc115d4d9b3\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"coverage\\\": [\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"States the selected compulsory route, extended parallel period and commencement date.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Background heading; creates no separate duty.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u2\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies the earlier circular, launch date, portal and application/submission context.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u3\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Explains parallel running and acceptance through existing channels.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u4\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Section heading linking extension and enhancements.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u5\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Describes monitoring and feedback; does not condition the compulsory route.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u6\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Extends parallel running through 29 November 2024 and explains its purpose.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u7\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Full-adoption heading supports the transition context.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u8\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Restates the compulsory route, describes integration of reporting requests and distinguishes optional fee settlement.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Enquiries heading; creates no submission requirement.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u10\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Practicability qualifies SFC operational enhancements; contact guidance creates no exception to the route.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies issuing division.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u12\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies issuing institution.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u13\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"End marker has no substantive effect.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies product categories associated with the IPD scope reference.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Expands WINGS; does not broaden the selected control.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u18\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dimensions\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The route applies to persons making applications or submissions concerning IPD-administered investment products. It is transaction-specific, with no bank-only actor limitation. The footnote identifies relevant product categories.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"definitions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"e-IP is the investment-product online application/submission system on WINGS. WINGS is expanded in footnote 2. The packet does not provide a complete test for classifying borderline communications as submissions or establish whether footnote 1 is an exhaustive taxonomy.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\",\\\"u18\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Existing-channel acceptance belongs to the parallel period, extended through 29 November. No post-transition exception is stated. 'where practicable' attaches to SFC review and enhancement, not submission duties; optional fee settlement is a separate facility.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"'must' imposes the selected submission-route requirement. 'can also' offers fee settlement. Statements about future integration and enhancements do not impose separate user duties or make commencement conditional on technical completion.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The original 29 October endpoint is replaced by 29 November 2024; compulsory routing starts on 30 November 2024 inclusively. The text does not resolve attempted-versus-completed submission timing or expressly explain treatment of pending cases.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"dependencies\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The 8 July 2024 launch circular and existing IPD submission requests supply referenced background whose full terms are absent. Dependency external-authorities.24ec50 has no supplied text or hash. These cannot establish additional exceptions, deadlines or filing duties.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Does the referenced launch circular specify how pending applications, supplementary documents and submissions attempted before but completed after 30 November 2024 are handled?\\\",\\n    \\\"Is footnote 1 an exhaustive restriction on product scope, or an identification of the products then administered by IPD?\\\",\\n    \\\"What determines the operative submission date, and which borderline communications qualify as submissions?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"readings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\n        \\\"Evaluate one application or submission event, not an institution's overall compliance.\\\",\\n        \\\"The extended parallel period retains the existing-channel acceptance described for parallel running.\\\",\\n        \\\"The operative submission date and product classification must be supplied from evidence; unknown values remain unknown.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\":[\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u4\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u7\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"The strongest supported reading uses the date of each submission event. For example, an in-scope supplementary submission made on 2 December for an application initially lodged on 28 November falls within the route requirement. A case-opening-date approach would exempt it, but this packet provides no affirmative support for that grandfathering rule, so it is an unresolved question rather than a second proposed reading. An ordinary existing-channel submission on 29 November remains within parallel running; the same event on 30 November engages the compulsory route. Optional annual-fee settlement does not independently engage this control.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The evaluated event is an application or submission concerning an investment product administered by IPD, assessed with the product categories in footnote 1. Optional fee payment alone does not establish this classification.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"is_ipd_product_application_or_submission\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"],\\n            \\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n            \\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean classification of the evaluated event\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The operative date on which the evaluated application or submission is made. The packet does not determine this date for incomplete or disputed transmission events.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"submission_date\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n            \\\"type\\\":\\\"date\\\",\\n            \\\"unit\\\":\\\"Gregorian calendar date\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The evaluated application or submission is submitted to IPD through e-IP.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"submitted_via_e_ip\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":false,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n            \\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n            \\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean route fact for the evaluated event\\\"\\n          }\\n        ],\\n        \\\"result\\\":\\\"submitted_via_e_ip\\\",\\n        \\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n        \\\"scope\\\":\\\"(and is_ipd_product_application_or_submission (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"r1\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\":[\\n        \\\"Does omitted transition guidance expressly preserve existing channels for subsequent submissions on already-open cases?\\\",\\n        \\\"For disputed transmission events, does submission occur on sending, receipt, acceptance or completion?\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"Selected control: compulsory e-IP submission route from 30 November 2024. Each in-scope application or submission made on or after that date must use e-IP. Existing-channel acceptance continues during the extended parallel period through 29 November. Neither planned enhancements nor the practicability qualification creates a stated exception. The result tests only route satisfaction within scope; it does not determine whether a filing is required, timely or substantively adequate.\\\",\\n      \\\"subject\\\":\\\"Route for an individual IPD investment-product application or submission\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":24593,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":2139,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":46}}\n","fresh_context":true,"independence":"CONTEXT_ONLY_SAME_MODEL_CORRELATION_UNMEASURED","model":"gpt-6-astra","provider":"codex.fresh.v1","provider_route_hash":"3d676052ff208f9c0b35467659af41d3138476127d0d1b523970689c2edf4714","request_hash":"c350082330b5956a4d3800f8f8b90757b36da9a12273918dba20209beae1991d","response_hash":"03c7d6a902a8d43f7c453efd5c77300e70390059ac4a4240ae5a22372f77e46d","transport_retry_policy":"NO_APPLICATION_RETRY; CLI transport behavior is external","usage":[{"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0,"input_tokens":24593,"output_tokens":2139,"reasoning_output_tokens":46}],"wall_milliseconds":79897},"response":{"coverage":[{"reason":"States the selected compulsory route, extended parallel period and commencement date.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading; creates no separate duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Identifies the earlier circular, launch date, portal and application/submission context.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Explains parallel running and acceptance through existing channels.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Section heading linking extension and enhancements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Describes monitoring and feedback; does not condition the compulsory route.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Extends parallel running through 29 November 2024 and explains its pur